node_modules/
dist/
*.log

# Secrets & local config — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
service-account.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
# WAL mode writes these two alongside the .sqlite, and neither matches `*.sqlite`. Without them a
# backup directory shows up as untracked — the whole DB, real owner data included, one `git add -A`
# from being committed. The WAL is not a scratch file either: it routinely holds megabytes of rows
# not yet checkpointed into the main file.
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
data/
backups/

# Your real Fly config. `fly.toml` in this repo is deliberately full of placeholders
# (`your-otto-server`) because the repo is public, and deploying with it would set
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN to a hostname that does not exist — which silently breaks every
# Google reconnect link, since those are built from it. Keep your real app name and
# origin here and deploy with `fly deploy -c fly.production.toml`.
fly.production.toml
